{
  "requirement": "Concurrent `verify` calls on the same domain keep separate dependency\nrecords and agent conversations, even for the same source node and criterion.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.verify.concurrent`.\n\nThe requirement has two obligations. Concurrent `verify` calls on one domain must keep separate dependency records, and they must keep separate agent conversations. Both must hold even when the source node and criterion are the same.\n\n**Agent conversations and dependency traces:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]`\n- It runs two `verify_with_agent` calls concurrently with `futures::join!` on one `Memory` graph.\n- Both calls use the `Question` criterion. Its `source_node_id` is always `Node(1)` and its `criterion_path` is always `[\"question\"]`. The two calls differ only in the agent context, `alpha` or `beta`. So this is the same source node and the same criterion.\n- The `ParallelConversations` provider uses a `Barrier(2)`, so the two conversations must be in flight at the same time. A 2-second timeout fails the test if either call blocks the other.\n- The provider asserts on every turn that the chat history length is `2 + turn*2`. It asserts the history contains only its own page contents and never the other conversation's. Both conversations use the tool call ID `same-call-id`, and the provider checks that the last delivered page belongs to its own conversation.\n- The test asserts three calls per conversation.\n- It stores the two results and loads the records. The `alpha` record has only the dependency on `Node(1)`. The `beta` record has the `OutgoingEdges` dependency on `Node(1)` plus the `Node(2)` content dependency. Neither record contains the other's dependencies.\n\n**Dependency records for the same source and criterion:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]`\n- Two `Review` criteria share source `Node(1)` and criterion path `[\"behavior\"]`. They differ in revision, output and reads (`Node(2)` versus `Node(3)`).\n- A barrier forces the two executions to overlap, and a 5-second timeout fails the test if they wait on each other.\n- It asserts each result's output. It asserts that nothing is written during `verify`, and that `store_evidence` is run for both.\n- The saved record is then checked as a whole. Its output, version and dependencies must all come from the same execution. The expected dependencies are a single `Node(2)` fingerprint \"first input\" for `first` and a single `Node(3)` fingerprint \"second input\" for `second`. Dependencies from the other execution would fail the assertion.\n- It also asserts two executions, two writes and one record.\n\nTogether the tests cover both obligations and the \"same node and criterion\" condition. A bug that mixed dependency traces or conversation histories between concurrent calls would fail these assertions. Both tests carry `{test}` references to the subject, so there is no marking gap.",
